# Sub-tick spin of the gem glint (tests/harness/check_feeder_subtick.sh --path
# glint-rot). Rows: <bk2> | <V> | rec=<addr> [rtol=] [step=]. rec is the pool
# record whose drawn orientation is judged, in sine-table entries modulo 64.
#
# sunrise-spring-surface-swim.bk2 1482, rec 8006DF48 (near star, 4.8 px
# extent): canon1480 8.86, canon1482 16.59, phase 138 to 146. With the replay
# rotating the corners against the routine's sense the alpha-0.5 ratio read
# 2.03; with the routine's sense 0.03 LERPED.
sunrise-spring-surface-swim.bk2 | 1482 | rec=8006DF48 rtol=0.25
# sunrise-spring-surface-swim.bk2 1284, rec 8006DF98 (near star, 10.5 px
# extent, the largest in the movie): canon1282 33.27, canon1284 41.41, phase 33
# to 41. 1.98 against the routine's sense, 0.02 with it.
sunrise-spring-surface-swim.bk2 | 1284 | rec=8006DF98 rtol=0.25
